---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Immigration Document Checklist Guide | AfriMigrate"
  description="How to gather police clearances, educational credential assessments and reference letters for your immigration application without losing months to delays."
>
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/blog">Blog</a> / Document Checklist Guide</div>
  <div class="eyebrow">Guide · Documents</div>
  <h1>The Immigration Document Checklist Guide</h1>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    Missing or delayed documents are the single biggest cause of slow immigration applications. Here's how to get ahead of every one of them.
  </p>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Start Here</div>
    <h2>The documents that take longest</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Document</th><th>Typical wait</th><th>Start it...</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Police clearance certificate</td><td>2–12 weeks</td><td>The day you decide to apply</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Educational Credential Assessment</td><td>4–12 weeks</td><td>Before you even calculate your score</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Language test results</td><td>Test + 1–2 weeks for results</td><td>As soon as you're ready to book</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Employer reference letters</td><td>Depends on employer responsiveness</td><td>While still employed, if possible</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Medical exam</td><td>Usually only after invitation</td><td>Only once instructed — results expire</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Common Mistakes</div>
    <h2>What slows people down</h2>
    <div class="tools-grid">
      <div class="tool-card"><div class="tool-icon">⏳</div><h3>Waiting for an invitation to start</h3><p>Most documents can and should be gathered before you're invited, not after.</p></div>
      <div class="tool-card"><div class="tool-icon">📝</div><h3>Vague reference letters</h3><p>Letters missing exact dates, hours per week, or duties get queried or rejected — be specific.</p></div>
      <div class="tool-card"><div class="tool-icon">🌍</div><h3>Forgetting past countries</h3><p>Police clearances are usually needed for every country you lived in for 6+ months since age 18, not just your current one.</p></div>
      <div class="tool-card"><div class="tool-icon">📅</div><h3>Letting documents expire</h3><p>Language test results and medical exams have validity windows — time them to your application stage.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Build Yours</div>
    <h2>Get your personalised checklist</h2>
    <a href="/canada/document-checklist" class="btn-primary" style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">Build my document checklist →</a>
  </section>
</Layout>
